<title>CANADA: Air Canada union says tentative deal reached.</title>
<headline>Air Canada union says tentative deal reached.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Union of Public Employees said on Thursday that it reached a tentative deal with Air Canada involving 4,600 flight attendants.</p>
<p>The union said that results of a ratification vote on the agreement would be announced on July 19 after a cross-country tour to present the deal to union members.</p>
<p>The union also said the deal would give the attendants a retroactive wage increase and allow the carrier to maintain operations.</p>
<p>&quot;The new contract represents the beginning of a new relationship between Air Canada flight attendants and their employer,&quot; said union local president, Baljit Salh.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
